            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "both decoupled trees have the lowest error of any method; on the harder, drift-dominated NOx response they are competitive with, though not ahead of, the deepest black-box models. A fully coupled coskewness tree is markedly worse on NOx, its skewness-aligned leaves generalizing poorly across the year boundary. This is exactly the gap the covariance leaves close.",
