                ],
                [
                    1084.0,
                    1050.0
                ],
                [
                    136.0,
                    1050.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Summarizing, the decoupled tbtree matches or beats every black-box baseline on scale-weighted error while remaining a single tree of 16 interpretable local emission models; the covariance leaves are what let the coskewness split compete predictively, whereas a fully coupled coskewness tree would trail in terms of predictive power.",
