        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "This paper has introduced tbtree, a shallow, deterministic and interpretable, top-down clustering tree that carries a local (dense or sparse) twoblock dimension reduction model in every leaf. To the author's knowledge it is the first tree-based regression method to do so, generalizing the PLS-Trees of Eriksson et al. (2009) from partial least squares to the joint predictor–response reduction of Cook et al. (2023). Its central methodological ingredient is a novel twoblock decomposition whose latent directions maximize the coskewness of the pre-",
